  "description": "Hummingbirds beat their wings up to about 80 times a second in a figure-eight pattern, so they push air down on the downstroke and the upstroke. That lets them hover in place and even fly backward. Their hearts can top 1,200 beats per minute, and at night they go into torpor to save energy. Ecuador has more than 100 species. Original 3D animation, wingbeats in slow motion.",
